---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kiln firing queues"
	description="Track bisque and glaze loads, charge firing fees by cubic inch, and text members when their pieces are ready for pickup."
>
	<section class="wrap section split">
		<div>
			<h1>Every piece, from shelf to pickup.</h1>
			<p class="lede muted">
				Members log a piece from their phone when they set it on the bisque shelf. Kilnbook measures
				it, charges the firing fee, puts it in the right load and tells them when it is cool enough
				to take home.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">See it on your kilns</a>
		</div>
		<img
			src="/images/firing-queue.svg"
			alt="A shelf queue for one kiln showing a bisque load at 70 percent and a cone 6 glaze load ready to fire"
			width="480"
			height="320"
		/>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Firing fees that add themselves up</h2>
		<p>
			Set a rate per cubic inch, a flat fee per piece, or both. Members enter height, width and depth
			(or pick a size from your presets: mug, bowl, large platter) and pay when they log the piece.
			No more counting pots on a shelf at the end of the month.
		</p>

		<h2>Loads that know what is in them</h2>
		<p>
			Each kiln has its own queue for bisque, cone 6 and cone 10 glaze firings. You can see how full
			each load is, move pieces between loads, and mark a load as fired with one tap. Kilnbook keeps a
			firing log for every kiln with the date, cone, schedule and who loaded it.
		</p>

		<h2>Pickup texts</h2>
		<p>
			When a load is unloaded, every member with work in it gets a text with a photo of the shelf.
			Pieces left for more than 30 days can trigger a polite reminder, then a storage fee if you
			want one.
		</p>

		<h2>How many kilns?</h2>
		<p>
			The Starter plan covers one kiln. The Studio plan covers up to 5 kilns, and Collective has no
			limit. Electric, gas and raku kilns all work the same way.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</Base>
